cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "timeseries_app_cookbook: A runnable template and recipe book for building interactive desktop apps that navigate and annotate long time series"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Zhao
    affiliation: "University of Rochester, Rochester, NY, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-5012"
abstract: >-
  A domain-neutral, runnable template for building interactive Dash and Plotly
  desktop applications that navigate, inspect, and annotate long time series
  smoothly, including recordings of millions of samples, using
  plotly-resampler. It is distilled from a production biomedical scoring
  application with every domain-specific detail removed, so that the signals
  shipped with it are synthetic and the reusable techniques are the substance:
  resampler-backed navigation, event coalescing for responsive panning and
  zooming, drag-to-select with automatic panning, keyboard annotation, undo,
  crash recovery, and running several recordings side by side. Adapting it to
  a new data type requires replacing one data-loading function and one
  configuration file. The accompanying README is written as a cookbook of
  numbered recipes, each pointing at the exact source file that implements it,
  and is intended to be read both by human developers and by coding agents
  adapting the template to a new scientific domain.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/timeseries_app_cookbook"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - time series
  - data visualization
  - annotation
  - desktop application
  - Dash
  - Plotly
  - research software
  - scientific software template
